109
00:04:21,492 --> 00:04:23,906
So the first secret is this.

110
00:04:24,086 --> 00:04:26,529
The most famous Ferrari of the nineteen

111
00:04:26,529 --> 00:04:28,784
eighties was not designed on a clean

112
00:04:28,784 --> 00:04:29,160
sheet.

113
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:32,237
It was assembled from a cancelled racing

114
00:04:32,237 --> 00:04:35,134
programme, an existing engine and a very

115
00:04:35,134 --> 00:04:37,958
short deadline, by a team that included

116
00:04:37,958 --> 00:04:39,986
Materazzi as chief engineer.

117
00:04:40,166 --> 00:04:44,284
Pininfarina's Pietro Camardella designed the body under

118
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:46,455
Aldo Brovarone's supervision,

119
00:04:46,455 --> 00:04:48,177
according to Wikipedia.

120
00:04:48,528 --> 00:04:50,304
Does that make it a lesser car?

121
00:04:50,484 --> 00:04:52,040
The evidence says no.

122
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:55,159
Wikipedia lists an independent test at four

123
00:04:55,159 --> 00:04:57,483
point seven seconds from zero to a

124
00:04:57,483 --> 00:05:00,080
hundred kilometres per hour with a top

125
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:03,361
speed of three hundred twenty-one kilometres per

126
00:05:03,361 --> 00:05:06,437
hour, about one hundred ninety-nine miles per

127
00:05:06,437 --> 00:05:06,779
hour.

128
00:05:06,959 --> 00:05:10,211
Road and Track measured three hundred fifteen,

129
00:05:10,211 --> 00:05:13,251
and Car and Driver three hundred seventeen.

130
00:05:13,431 --> 00:05:15,969
A quick project does not mean a

131
00:05:15,969 --> 00:05:16,705
slow car.

132
00:05:17,056 --> 00:05:18,960
The archive page goes further.

133
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:21,138
It says the F forty was the

134
00:05:21,138 --> 00:05:24,099
first production car to pass two hundred

135
00:05:24,099 --> 00:05:25,210
miles per hour,

136
00:05:25,210 --> 00:05:26,616
at two hundred one.

137
00:05:26,796 --> 00:05:28,384
The Wikipedia page,

138
00:05:28,384 --> 00:05:32,060
by contrast, lists measured top speeds below

139
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:36,155
two hundred, one ninety-six and one ninety-seven,

140
00:05:36,155 --> 00:05:37,826
from magazine tests.

141
00:05:38,006 --> 00:05:40,526
A claim and a measurement are different

142
00:05:40,526 --> 00:05:40,978
things.

143
00:05:41,158 --> 00:05:42,127
We report both,

144
00:05:42,127 --> 00:05:44,001
and we note that the claim is

145
00:05:44,001 --> 00:05:46,069
the one that made the headlines.

146
00:05:46,419 --> 00:05:47,870
Now the second secret.

147
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:50,917
Wikipedia describes the interior.

148
00:05:51,097 --> 00:05:54,534
The cars had moderate air conditioning but

149
00:05:54,534 --> 00:05:55,843
no sound system,

150
00:05:55,843 --> 00:05:57,152
no door handles,

151
00:05:57,152 --> 00:05:58,215
no glove box,

152
00:05:58,215 --> 00:06:00,997
no leather, no carpets and no door

153
00:06:00,997 --> 00:06:01,570
panels.

154
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:04,608
The first fifty cars had sliding Lexan

155
00:06:04,608 --> 00:06:05,209
