165
00:06:26,181 --> 00:06:29,649
a tubular steel chassis with bonded composite

166
00:06:29,649 --> 00:06:33,348
inserts, and a ventilated Plexiglas rear screen.

167
00:06:33,528 --> 00:06:35,988
It calls the F forty the first

168
00:06:35,988 --> 00:06:39,186
car whose bodywork was made entirely of

169
00:06:39,186 --> 00:06:40,088
composites.

170
00:06:40,438 --> 00:06:42,342
Weight shows the result.

171
00:06:42,522 --> 00:06:44,646
Wikipedia lists one thousand,

172
00:06:44,646 --> 00:06:48,088
two hundred fifty-four kilograms for Europe and

173
00:06:48,088 --> 00:06:51,458
one thousand, three hundred sixty-nine for the

174
00:06:51,458 --> 00:06:52,483
United States.

175
00:06:52,663 --> 00:06:54,950
The archive says one thousand,

176
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,169
two hundred two.

177
00:06:56,349 --> 00:07:00,154
Classic Motorsports says about three thousand pounds

178
00:07:00,154 --> 00:07:01,324
for the U S car,

179
00:07:01,324 --> 00:07:03,373
which is about one thousand,

180
00:07:03,373 --> 00:07:05,567
three hundred sixty kilograms.

181
00:07:05,747 --> 00:07:07,215
Three different weights,

182
00:07:07,215 --> 00:07:09,540
and the differences are over a hundred

183
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:10,763
and fifty kilograms.

184
00:07:11,113 --> 00:07:12,866
Here is the twist about price.

185
00:07:13,046 --> 00:07:15,946
Wikipedia says the launch price was about

186
00:07:15,946 --> 00:07:18,068
four hundred thousand dollars,

187
00:07:18,068 --> 00:07:20,544
roughly five times the price of the

188
00:07:20,544 --> 00:07:22,170
